1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,712
♪ <i>Oh, Mister Tailor…</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,795 --> 00:00:09,050
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

3
00:00:09,134 --> 00:00:10,844
♪ <i>Oh, Mister Tailor…</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:12,887
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut and it’s done.</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:18,601
[Atoy] <i>What is this doing here?</i>

7
00:00:18,685 --> 00:00:20,103
<i>Son of a thread.</i>

8
00:00:20,186 --> 00:00:22,480
<i>So this is where they're hiding these.</i>

9
00:00:22,564 --> 00:00:23,356
[Samir] <i>Okay, gentlemen.</i>

10
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:28,278
<i>You have one job today, and that is</i>
<i>to bring these crates to the yacht.</i>

11
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:31,781
<i>And do not open these crates.</i>

12
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:34,284
[Atoy] <i>What are they going to use</i>
<i>this much gold for?</i>

13
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:36,244
<i>"Where are we going to place</i>
<i>all the gold?"</i>

14
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:37,954
[Samir] <i>In the office.</i>

15
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:39,664
But only for a short time.

16
00:00:39,748 --> 00:00:41,833
<i>We have to exchange it for cash.</i>

17
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:42,876
What are you doing here?

18
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:44,669
[Alvin] <i>Someone knocked me out…</i>

19
00:00:44,753 --> 00:00:46,004
[On the phone] <i>…on the way to the yacht!</i>

20
00:00:46,588 --> 00:00:47,672
He could be a policeman!

21
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:49,883
One of the transporters is an intruder!

22
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:51,050
[Audrey] <i>Gavin, why are you leaving?</i>

23
00:00:51,134 --> 00:00:52,844
No one is asking you to leave.

24
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:55,597
I don't want to force
myself to stay here anymore.

25
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:59,893
There seems to be a shark here
in a dolphin suit.

26
00:00:59,976 --> 00:01:01,561
<i>Remove your masks.</i>

27
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:03,605
[bullets whizzing]

28
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:09,027
[music continues…]

29
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:09,986
Who are you?

30
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,362
What are you doing here?

31
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:12,530
Oka?

32
00:01:12,614 --> 00:01:14,157
[Samir] <i>I know you're here.</i>

33
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:15,408
<i>You are an imposter!</i>

34
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:16,451
[music swells]

35
00:01:16,534 --> 00:01:17,619
[Atoy] <i>I'm not that stupid, Samir.</i>

36
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:19,871
I knew it was you.

37
00:01:19,954 --> 00:01:21,039
Where did you bring my boss?

38
00:01:21,122 --> 00:01:21,998
Business.

39
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:24,042
[swishing and clanging]

40
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:25,794
[thumping and thudding]

41
00:01:25,877 --> 00:01:27,879
[Janine] <i>Who's that with him, Mommy?</i>

42
00:01:27,962 --> 00:01:30,298
It looks like they're best friends.

43
00:01:30,381 --> 00:01:31,257
I don't know him.

44
00:01:31,341 --> 00:01:33,718
[Ibyang] <i>I wonder</i>
<i>where Tatoy's best friend is.</i>

45
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:35,053
- [grunts and groans]
- [clangs and thuds]

46
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:41,976
[Artem] <i>Sir, what about the gold?!</i>

47
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:44,187
- Leave the gold! The ship is going down!
- [grunts]

48
00:01:44,270 --> 00:01:46,523
- [Atoy] <i>Oka?</i>
- [Oscar] <i>We need to leave now.</i>

49
00:01:48,608 --> 00:01:51,069
Atoy is very slippery.

50
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:53,238
He cheated death many, many times.

51
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:55,240
And I will not stop.

52
00:01:55,323 --> 00:01:59,577
[Samir] <i>…until I see</i>
<i>his rotten corpse in the grave.</i>

53
00:02:00,161 --> 00:02:00,829
Oka!

54
00:02:03,581 --> 00:02:05,583
Mmm. Neckline, sixteen.

55
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:09,629
What is this halter dress for
that you're having made, Denden?

56
00:02:10,213 --> 00:02:11,464
Nothing. I just thought of it.

57
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:15,802
So I have something new to wear
when Emerson and I go on a date, my love!

58
00:02:15,885 --> 00:02:18,221
A halter dress for a date?

59
00:02:18,304 --> 00:02:22,267
It seems like Emerson is only going
to take you out to the siomai stand.

60
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:24,602
- [pleasant music playing]
- [Denden] Ms. Cita and Ame…

61
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:27,730
Of course, it's the thought
that counts, right?

62
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:31,484
No matter where Emerson takes me,
I'll be happy.

63
00:02:31,985 --> 00:02:32,986
Length, twenty-nine.

64
00:02:33,069 --> 00:02:34,821
[Denden chuckles]

65
00:02:34,904 --> 00:02:35,905
Hi, Ame!

66
00:02:35,989 --> 00:02:38,366
Ah, Ms. Cita, where's Atoy?

67
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:40,535
Oh. He's not here, Audrey.

68
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:42,328
Didn't he drive you to work today?

69
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:44,956
No. I took the service vehicle.

70
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:47,333
Too bad. I thought I'd see him here.

71
00:02:47,417 --> 00:02:49,711
- [Cita] Ahh.
- So, he left already.

72
00:02:49,794 --> 00:02:51,379
I wonder where Atoy went.

73
00:02:52,088 --> 00:02:55,383
[sneaky music playing]

74
00:02:55,466 --> 00:02:58,344
Where's… Jesabel?

75
00:02:59,262 --> 00:03:02,015
She hasn't been here all morning.

76
00:03:02,098 --> 00:03:03,516
Do you think they're together?

77
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:22,452
[foreboding music playing]

78
00:03:40,929 --> 00:03:42,138
Oka.

79
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:47,560
Help! Help!

80
00:03:51,272 --> 00:03:52,774
Help! Over here!

81
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:01,866
[music fades…]

82
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:05,995
[theme music playing]

83
00:04:06,079 --> 00:04:08,873
♪ <i>Oh, Mister Tailor…</i> ♪

84
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:11,084
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

85
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:16,631
♪ <i>Wait a moment, Mister Tailor</i> ♪

86
00:04:16,714 --> 00:04:17,966
♪ <i>Can you be the one to sew</i> ♪

87
00:04:18,049 --> 00:04:21,344
♪ <i>My polo’s hole that's right</i>
<i>under the armpit</i> ♪

88
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:23,596
♪ <i>In every cut of cloth</i> ♪

89
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,932
♪ <i>There's a secret behind it</i> ♪

90
00:04:26,015 --> 00:04:27,850
♪ <i>If your measurement is wrong</i> ♪

91
00:04:27,934 --> 00:04:31,521
♪ <i>The whole fit turns crooked…</i> ♪

92
00:04:31,604 --> 00:04:33,106
[gunshots]

93
00:04:33,189 --> 00:04:34,857
♪ <i>Oh, Mister Tailor</i> ♪

94
00:04:34,941 --> 00:04:37,402
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

95
00:04:37,485 --> 00:04:38,569
[music swells]

96
00:04:40,571 --> 00:04:41,990
[music fades…]

97
00:04:42,073 --> 00:04:44,993
[man's voice] <i>What do you mean</i>
<i>the Grey Shadow is gone?</i>

98
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:46,911
There was an explosion.

99
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:47,829
[heavy music playing]

100
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:50,540
All the guns, they're all gone.

101
00:04:50,623 --> 00:04:53,042
Everything. The gold, all gone.

102
00:04:54,919 --> 00:04:57,714
[Man's voice] <i>I see your failure</i>
<i>as a betrayal of trust.</i>

103
00:04:57,797 --> 00:04:59,549
<i>And I hate people who betray me.</i>

104
00:04:59,632 --> 00:05:01,175
<i>You should know that!</i>

105
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:03,761
Sorry, Sir.

106
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:07,765
Don't worry. The plan will proceed.

107
00:05:07,849 --> 00:05:10,018
The men will retrieve the gold.

108
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:15,189
[Man's voice] <i>I will give you a chance</i>
<i>to clean up your mess, Samir.</i>

109
00:05:15,273 --> 00:05:19,402
<i>If you fail again, you will find yourself</i>
<i>in the same position as the Grey Shadow.</i>

110
00:05:19,485 --> 00:05:21,029
[suspicious music playing]

111
00:05:21,863 --> 00:05:22,905
[phone blips]

112
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:28,745
[speaking in Russian] Damn it!

113
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:37,712
If Atoy survives the crash,
he will not survive me.

114
00:05:37,795 --> 00:05:40,882
[tense music playing]

115
00:05:48,639 --> 00:05:52,226
[music swells]

116
00:05:57,899 --> 00:05:59,275
[music fades…]

117
00:05:59,358 --> 00:06:01,527
Atoy, you're not answering.

118
00:06:01,611 --> 00:06:04,697
Why don't you call Emerson?
Maybe they're together.

119
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:06,199
Okay, good idea.

120
00:06:06,282 --> 00:06:08,951
[pensive music playing]

121
00:06:12,163 --> 00:06:13,831
[line rings]

122
00:06:13,915 --> 00:06:15,333
Hello, Emerson?

123
00:06:15,416 --> 00:06:16,709
Oh, hello, Audrey.

124
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:18,628
[Emerson on the phone] <i>Well…</i>

125
00:06:19,128 --> 00:06:21,631
I'm not with Atoy.

126
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:27,303
Maybe… maybe he's with a client.

127
00:06:27,386 --> 00:06:29,263
Or maybe he’s… he’s…

128
00:06:29,347 --> 00:06:30,932
- [Jesabel] Emerson!
- … delivering a suit. Yes, that's it.

129
00:06:31,015 --> 00:06:32,433
- [Jesabel] <i>I'm starving already.</i>
- [Emerson] <i>Maybe that's it.</i>

130
00:06:32,517 --> 00:06:33,392
<i>Let's go eat!</i>

131
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:35,478
Oh, it’s not allowed?

132
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:38,106
Who's there with you?

133
00:06:38,189 --> 00:06:40,108
Ah, it's just Jesabel. Jesabel.

134
00:06:40,191 --> 00:06:41,234
Ahh.

135
00:06:41,317 --> 00:06:45,488
So you're with Jesabel? Okay!

136
00:06:45,571 --> 00:06:47,740
[Audrey on the phone] <i>Good to know.</i>
<i>Thank you!</i>

137
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:49,992
Okay. Bye, Audrey. Bye.

138
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:50,952
[Jesabel] That was Audrey?

139
00:06:51,619 --> 00:06:54,122
Jesabel? Who's that?

140
00:06:54,622 --> 00:07:00,211
[rousing music playing]

141
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:03,631
[ambulance siren wailing in the distance]

142
00:07:04,674 --> 00:07:06,592
- [tense music playing]
- [nurse] What happened to him?

143
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:09,637
He got into an accident
on the ship we were on.

144
00:07:10,346 --> 00:07:11,180
Oka!

145
00:07:11,264 --> 00:07:12,849
We're at the hospital now.

146
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:14,767
You're safe.

147
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:17,103
[music swells]

148
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:21,065
That was Samir and his men.

149
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:25,695
[sneaky music playing]

150
00:07:25,778 --> 00:07:27,738
Wait. Why are there only two of them?

151
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:28,948
Where's Atoy?

152
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:29,866
And where are the others?

153
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:31,242
[Coastguard] Come with me first.

154
00:07:31,325 --> 00:07:33,870
There was an unusual explosion
in the middle of the sea.

155
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:37,999
Oh, what did he say?

156
00:07:38,082 --> 00:07:40,293
An unusual explosion?

157
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:42,795
[Jesabel] An unusual explosion?

158
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:45,423
Wait. What would explode
in the middle of the sea?

159
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:48,509
- Maybe it's just your armpit.
- Huh?

160
00:07:49,552 --> 00:07:51,095
You got some nerve.

161
00:07:51,179 --> 00:07:54,599
I can compete with any model out there.

162
00:07:54,682 --> 00:07:55,558
The nerve of you.

163
00:07:55,641 --> 00:07:58,936
Yeah, when I get a deodorant commercial.

164
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:00,605
Excuse me.

165
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:02,482
All right, all right. Of course.

166
00:08:03,524 --> 00:08:05,568
What did they even do out at sea?

167
00:08:05,651 --> 00:08:07,612
- [sneaky music playing]
- And where is Atoy?

168
00:08:08,112 --> 00:08:09,864
Come on, let's follow them.

169
00:08:09,947 --> 00:08:10,948
- Follow where?
- Come on.

170
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:12,366
Let's go check them out.

171
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:14,452
I'm tired already.

172
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:20,500
[music fades…]

173
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:33,721
[electronic blipping]

174
00:08:35,681 --> 00:08:37,391
The hostages have been moved, Atoy.

175
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:39,393
What? Let's go?

176
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:41,938
Son of a--

177
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:45,233
We're really charging in,
just the two of us?

178
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:47,818
Won't this get us killed?

179
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:49,779
Come on.

180
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:55,034
You know anything is possible
as long as we have each other's backs.

181
00:08:58,287 --> 00:09:00,957
Do you have your Saint Anthony of Padua?

182
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:04,085
[sound]

183
00:09:06,087 --> 00:09:07,338
Sorry, Atoy.

184
00:09:08,089 --> 00:09:08,965
[Oscar] The chain broke.

185
00:09:09,048 --> 00:09:12,260
It got caught on a nail
in the barracks bathroom.

186
00:09:12,343 --> 00:09:14,637
I was in such a hurry,
I never got around to fixing it.

187
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:16,931
Here.

188
00:09:18,516 --> 00:09:21,936
[pensive music playing]

189
00:09:31,195 --> 00:09:32,405
A fisherman's knot.

190
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:33,990
That's durable.

191
00:09:35,074 --> 00:09:37,827
Make sure you never
take it off your neck again.

192
00:09:38,661 --> 00:09:40,538
Because when you pray,

193
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:44,000
you won't just find lost things,

194
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,335
but also… [smirks]

195
00:09:46,419 --> 00:09:49,213
people who've lost themselves
and lost their minds.

196
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:51,465
[chuckles]

197
00:09:54,218 --> 00:09:55,344
Does this really work?

198
00:09:56,053 --> 00:09:56,929
Of course.

199
00:09:57,013 --> 00:09:58,139
[smirks]

200
00:09:58,222 --> 00:10:00,600
So, what?
If I go missing during this operation…

201
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:04,729
does this have a GPS
that tells you where I am?

202
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:06,731
If you disappear during an operation,

203
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:10,318
no matter what corner of the world
you end up in, I'll find you.

204
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:12,486
No one gets left behind.

205
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:14,322
[melodramatic music playing]

206
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:15,740
Thanks, 'Toy.

207
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:18,284
No one gets left behind.

208
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,787
[music fades…]

209
00:10:24,332 --> 00:10:28,836
[melancholic music playing]

210
00:10:38,012 --> 00:10:39,013
[coughs]

211
00:10:39,096 --> 00:10:40,056
[clears throat]

212
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:46,437
Atoy?

213
00:10:47,563 --> 00:10:49,190
[coughs]

214
00:10:49,273 --> 00:10:50,274
[clears throat]

215
00:10:50,858 --> 00:10:53,486
Is that… is that you?

216
00:10:53,569 --> 00:10:55,738
[music continues…]

217
00:10:56,947 --> 00:11:00,242
[coughing]

218
00:11:01,243 --> 00:11:02,078
[groans]

219
00:11:04,622 --> 00:11:07,375
Buddy, I dreamt about you.

220
00:11:08,918 --> 00:11:11,337
[clears throat] I was drowning and…

221
00:11:11,962 --> 00:11:13,255
you saved me.

222
00:11:15,716 --> 00:11:17,134
That wasn't a dream, buddy.

223
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:20,179
It was really me.

224
00:11:22,765 --> 00:11:24,809
I saved you, Oka.

225
00:11:25,309 --> 00:11:26,435
[chuckles softly]

226
00:11:28,104 --> 00:11:29,271
[Atoy] But the truth is…

227
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:33,025
Bro, you saved me first.

228
00:11:33,859 --> 00:11:34,735
Huh?

229
00:11:37,196 --> 00:11:38,989
[explosion and rumbling nearby]

230
00:11:39,073 --> 00:11:40,950
'Toy, Atoy.

231
00:11:41,659 --> 00:11:42,910
Psst, hey.

232
00:11:42,993 --> 00:11:45,204
[fire crackling and rumbling]

233
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:49,333
I knew it, you were the one I saw earlier.

234
00:11:52,169 --> 00:11:53,129
Oka?

235
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:55,589
This ship is sinking.
We need to leave now.

236
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:58,467
[fire crackling and rumbling]

237
00:11:58,551 --> 00:11:59,885
Son of a thread.

238
00:12:01,178 --> 00:12:02,012
Okay.

239
00:12:05,808 --> 00:12:09,437
After that, I helped you,
there in the water.

240
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:12,815
[tense music playing]

241
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:15,985
After the Grey Shadow ship exploded.

242
00:12:16,068 --> 00:12:18,904
[soft drama music playing]

243
00:12:22,658 --> 00:12:24,285
Buddy…

244
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:26,287
this is yours, isn't it?

245
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:42,511
Buddy, what were you doing on that ship?

246
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:46,056
What do you know about Grey Shadow?

247
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:47,224
Why were you there?

248
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:51,103
And why do you know Samir?

249
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:55,774
[heavy music playing]

250
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:59,320
Buddy, I was so shocked
when I saw you there.

251
00:12:59,403 --> 00:13:00,988
Just think about it.

252
00:13:01,822 --> 00:13:04,074
It's been more than ten years
since we last saw each other.

253
00:13:04,158 --> 00:13:06,702
More than ten years since
we were last together,

254
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:08,579
and then suddenly you show up.

255
00:13:09,497 --> 00:13:10,873
And you were there of all places.

256
00:13:11,373 --> 00:13:12,875
Buddy, what happened to you?

257
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:13,959
[pensive music playing]

258
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:14,919
[Atoy] What…

259
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:18,005
What happened, buddy?

260
00:13:18,088 --> 00:13:20,174
Were you the captain of that ship?

261
00:13:20,257 --> 00:13:23,552
Bro, I never wanted to be there.

262
00:13:27,014 --> 00:13:31,727
If only you knew, bro,
everything I've been through.

263
00:13:32,686 --> 00:13:36,690
Do you still remember
the last operation we worked on together?

264
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:38,734
[Oscar] Hmm?

265
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:43,197
- [explosions and rumbling]
- [tense music playing]

266
00:13:45,449 --> 00:13:49,245
- [gunshots]
- [groans]

267
00:14:06,971 --> 00:14:08,222
Help us!

268
00:14:15,062 --> 00:14:17,231
[groans]

269
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:19,733
Move, move, move, move!

270
00:14:19,817 --> 00:14:20,860
Move!

271
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:22,027
[tense music playing]

272
00:14:22,111 --> 00:14:24,280
Sister, over here.

273
00:14:32,037 --> 00:14:32,913
Sister Carmel.

274
00:14:36,458 --> 00:14:37,668
Mr. Drilon…

275
00:14:38,711 --> 00:14:40,045
I’m Captain Oscar Asuncion.

276
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:42,882
We're here to rescue you.

277
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:44,758
Let's go.

278
00:14:48,053 --> 00:14:51,265
[suspenseful music playing]

279
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:53,601
[bomb blips]

280
00:14:58,105 --> 00:14:59,940
Asuncion, subjects are secured.

281
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:02,067
[Atoy] I repeat. Subjects are secured.

282
00:15:02,151 --> 00:15:04,236
Proceed to the rally point immediately.

283
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:05,362
Copy?

284
00:15:05,446 --> 00:15:07,323
[ominous music playing]

285
00:15:07,406 --> 00:15:10,034
Sir, there are more coming.

286
00:15:10,117 --> 00:15:11,493
There are many of them. We have to move.

287
00:15:12,244 --> 00:15:14,121
[Atoy] You go ahead to the rally point.
I'll follow.

288
00:15:14,204 --> 00:15:15,539
I'll wait for Asuncion.

289
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:17,333
- Move!
- Copy, Sir.

290
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:26,050
[music swells]

291
00:15:28,385 --> 00:15:29,678
[Atoy] <i>Oka, Oka, come in.</i>

292
00:15:29,762 --> 00:15:30,596
[tense music playing]

293
00:15:30,679 --> 00:15:32,139
Subjects are secured.

294
00:15:32,222 --> 00:15:33,724
Where are you?

295
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:40,856
Oka, come in.

296
00:15:42,107 --> 00:15:43,734
I'm coming for you.

297
00:15:43,817 --> 00:15:45,486
What are you waiting for?

298
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:47,571
Go to the rally point now.

299
00:15:48,072 --> 00:15:49,531
Sir, you're alone.

300
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:51,075
Go now.

301
00:15:51,158 --> 00:15:52,618
I'm not leaving Asuncion behind.

302
00:15:52,701 --> 00:15:53,702
Move!

303
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:55,329
Copy, Sir. Let's go.

304
00:15:56,288 --> 00:15:57,748
Oka, Oka, come in.

305
00:15:57,831 --> 00:16:01,043
[Oscar on the radio]
<i>Padua, I'm surrounded by hostiles.</i>

306
00:16:01,126 --> 00:16:02,544
<i>Bomb my location.</i>

307
00:16:02,628 --> 00:16:04,338
What? No.

308
00:16:04,421 --> 00:16:05,506
I'm coming to get you.

309
00:16:05,589 --> 00:16:07,967
[Oscar on the radio] <i>No.</i>
<i>Don't come back for me.</i>

310
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:10,302
<i>I'm as good as dead.</i>

311
00:16:10,803 --> 00:16:12,179
- [fizz of radio static]
- <i>-Save our unit.</i>

312
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:14,723
<i>Just bomb my location.</i>

313
00:16:14,807 --> 00:16:15,683
<i>Do you copy?</i>

314
00:16:15,766 --> 00:16:18,060
[fizz of radio static]

315
00:16:18,143 --> 00:16:21,146
[melodramatic music playing]

316
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:23,065
[Oscar on the radio] <i>Do you copy, Padua?</i>

317
00:16:23,148 --> 00:16:24,066
<i>Respond!</i>

318
00:16:24,149 --> 00:16:26,443
[fizz of radio static]

319
00:16:26,527 --> 00:16:28,529
Copy.

320
00:16:28,612 --> 00:16:32,241
[Oscar on the radio] <i>It's been an honor</i>
<i>serving our country with you, Padua.</i>

321
00:16:33,951 --> 00:16:35,411
The honor was mine, brother.

322
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:50,259
Striker One, this is Captain Padua.

323
00:16:52,886 --> 00:16:54,096
Initiate air strike.

324
00:16:54,179 --> 00:16:58,642
[music swells]

325
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:00,519
[music fades…]

326
00:17:01,478 --> 00:17:04,565
[dramatic music playing]

327
00:17:07,317 --> 00:17:11,780
[sound]

328
00:17:11,864 --> 00:17:13,032
Do you have visual?

329
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:19,288
[Soldier on the radio]
<i>This is from the ground unit.</i>

330
00:17:19,371 --> 00:17:20,497
<i>Units are secured.</i>

331
00:17:20,581 --> 00:17:22,708
<i>Engage air strike on the main rebel camp.</i>

332
00:17:22,791 --> 00:17:23,709
Execute.

333
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:29,506
[missile passing overhead]

334
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:32,051
[explosion and rumbling nearby]

335
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:33,510
[music fades…]

336
00:17:33,594 --> 00:17:37,723
I wasn't the one who radioed
you to bomb my position.

337
00:17:38,223 --> 00:17:40,267
[pensive music playing]

338
00:17:40,350 --> 00:17:42,561
I never gave that order, ‘Toy.

339
00:17:44,396 --> 00:17:45,355
They had already captured me.

340
00:17:45,439 --> 00:17:46,774
There was nothing I could do.

341
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:49,234
[heavy music playing]

342
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:51,111
Who are they?

343
00:17:51,612 --> 00:17:52,738
Who are they?

344
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:54,531
Bro, who are they?

345
00:17:54,615 --> 00:17:56,992
The Obsidian operatives.

346
00:17:59,161 --> 00:18:01,246
They found me there, still breathing.

347
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:03,332
They were actually working
with the Red Front.

348
00:18:04,541 --> 00:18:06,877
They made me speak into a…

349
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:08,212
a device,

350
00:18:09,379 --> 00:18:12,132
so they could imitate my voice.

351
00:18:13,675 --> 00:18:16,804
One of their men was the one
who radioed you and told you to bomb us.

352
00:18:23,977 --> 00:18:26,271
[sighs] That explains it.

353
00:18:26,355 --> 00:18:29,983
That explains why, when the rescue team
came back to retrieve the bodies

354
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:31,568
of our comrades who died…

355
00:18:32,861 --> 00:18:34,279
your body wasn't there.

356
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:36,156
[pensive music playing]

357
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:38,408
They searched for your body.

358
00:18:38,492 --> 00:18:41,286
They found nothing,
so you were presumed dead.

359
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:44,456
- Killed in action.
- Killed in action? I was alive, 'Toy.

360
00:18:46,416 --> 00:18:47,793
I was alive.

361
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:50,129
[Oscar] But honestly…

362
00:18:51,547 --> 00:18:54,341
I wish they had just let me die there.

363
00:18:54,424 --> 00:18:56,301
Because after that night…

364
00:18:57,761 --> 00:18:59,221
I was still breathing…

365
00:19:00,889 --> 00:19:01,974
but for what?

366
00:19:04,226 --> 00:19:06,061
To become their slave?

367
00:19:07,396 --> 00:19:08,647
What do you mean, "slave"?

368
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,691
What did they do to you, buddy?

369
00:19:11,191 --> 00:19:12,985
[tense music playing]

370
00:19:13,068 --> 00:19:14,361
You're stubborn, aren't you?!

371
00:19:18,782 --> 00:19:19,825
Hit him!

372
00:19:19,908 --> 00:19:21,451
[thumping]

373
00:19:22,536 --> 00:19:24,371
[grunting and groaning]

374
00:19:24,454 --> 00:19:26,373
[grunts]

375
00:19:27,499 --> 00:19:29,626
[Oscar] <i>Every time I made a mistake,</i>

376
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:31,837
<i>or did something they didn't like,</i>

377
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:34,381
<i>they hurt me repeatedly.</i>

378
00:19:34,464 --> 00:19:36,508
<i>Nonstop, over and over.</i>

379
00:19:36,592 --> 00:19:39,261
<i>- They hurt me. They broke me.</i>
- [grunts]

380
00:19:39,887 --> 00:19:41,763
[thumps]

381
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:44,725
[melodramatic music playing]

382
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:53,650
[clatters, then thuds]

383
00:19:54,526 --> 00:19:56,403
- [dramatic music playing]
- [whip cracks]

384
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:58,530
[grunts and growls]

385
00:19:59,114 --> 00:20:01,700
[Oscar] <i>How was I supposed to fight?</i>
<i>How was I supposed to escape?</i>

386
00:20:02,784 --> 00:20:05,412
<i>They threatened me.</i>
<i>They said they'd drag my family into it.</i>

387
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:09,583
[Oscar] <i>They started with my sister, bro.</i>

388
00:20:10,083 --> 00:20:11,043
<i>Even my parents, bro.</i>

389
00:20:11,126 --> 00:20:12,836
<i>They said they'd kill them.</i>

390
00:20:13,670 --> 00:20:16,215
<i>Everyone important to me, bro.</i>

391
00:20:16,298 --> 00:20:17,758
<i>They were going to kill them all.</i>

392
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:21,053
So, I just endured it,

393
00:20:21,136 --> 00:20:23,805
I endured the suffering
they put me through.

394
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:25,557
[pensive music playing]

395
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:28,727
I endured becoming lower than an animal.

396
00:20:32,231 --> 00:20:34,566
Lower than an animal, bro.

397
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:37,402
[Oscar] Because what else could I do?

398
00:20:37,986 --> 00:20:41,031
Nobody came to help me. Nobody came.

399
00:20:42,616 --> 00:20:44,117
[Oscar] But it should have been you.

400
00:20:45,535 --> 00:20:47,079
I thought…

401
00:20:47,955 --> 00:20:49,957
I thought we never leave anyone behind.

402
00:20:50,457 --> 00:20:51,333
Hmm?

403
00:20:52,167 --> 00:20:53,043
[music fades…]

404
00:20:53,126 --> 00:20:54,503
I'm sorry.

405
00:20:54,586 --> 00:20:56,922
[soft drama music playing]

406
00:20:57,005 --> 00:20:58,757
Bro, I'm sorry.

407
00:21:00,884 --> 00:21:02,427
[Atoy] I really thought you were the one…

408
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:05,389
Yes, you were the one I was
talking to on the radio.

409
00:21:07,182 --> 00:21:08,058
Bro…

410
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:10,477
I was wrong.

411
00:21:11,436 --> 00:21:12,479
I'm sorry, brother.

412
00:21:14,147 --> 00:21:15,274
I should have come back for you.

413
00:21:15,357 --> 00:21:16,984
Hmm.

414
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:19,569
Bro, that's what I was going to do.

415
00:21:22,614 --> 00:21:23,824
I made a mistake.

416
00:21:24,324 --> 00:21:27,411
Because of that wrong
assumption of yours, bro, you know…

417
00:21:27,911 --> 00:21:30,497
more than ten years of my life
were destroyed.

418
00:21:31,915 --> 00:21:35,210
[tense music playing]

419
00:21:40,424 --> 00:21:42,009
But then again…

420
00:21:45,178 --> 00:21:46,722
Now, I understand why…

421
00:21:46,805 --> 00:21:47,723
[sniffles]

422
00:21:48,515 --> 00:21:51,059
Why you chose to leave me there.

423
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:52,728
[soft drama music playing]

424
00:21:52,811 --> 00:21:54,396
Because you heard it, right?

425
00:21:54,479 --> 00:21:56,148
You heard a direct command coming from me.

426
00:21:58,317 --> 00:22:05,032
Of course, the safety of the hostages
was more important, right?

427
00:22:09,911 --> 00:22:11,455
If only you knew, bro.

428
00:22:13,749 --> 00:22:15,125
That was one of the…

429
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:18,503
hardest decisions I ever made, Oka.

430
00:22:22,632 --> 00:22:24,051
I should never have left you there.

431
00:22:24,134 --> 00:22:26,511
[melodramatic music playing]

432
00:22:26,595 --> 00:22:28,388
Buddy…

433
00:22:30,682 --> 00:22:32,893
you know I could never do that to you.

434
00:22:34,603 --> 00:22:35,645
I'm sorry, buddy.

435
00:22:38,982 --> 00:22:40,859
[Oscar sighs]

436
00:22:40,942 --> 00:22:44,571
I really thought you wanted to save us…

437
00:22:45,072 --> 00:22:46,907
that's why I followed your order.

438
00:22:49,409 --> 00:22:52,204
[Atoy] All along, I thought it was
you I was speaking to.

439
00:22:52,287 --> 00:22:53,789
[music fades…]

440
00:22:54,873 --> 00:22:55,749
Sorry.

441
00:22:57,793 --> 00:22:59,252
- [soft drama music playing]
- Uhm…

442
00:22:59,961 --> 00:23:00,921
[sniffles]

443
00:23:01,713 --> 00:23:03,548
I understand you, bro.

444
00:23:05,133 --> 00:23:07,260
Really, I do. I understand.

445
00:23:09,221 --> 00:23:11,973
So, I hope you don't think that…

446
00:23:13,183 --> 00:23:15,227
even until now, I’m still blaming you.

447
00:23:18,188 --> 00:23:20,065
That's all in the past. [chuckles softly]

448
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:23,193
What matters is the present, right?

449
00:23:25,946 --> 00:23:26,780
Right?

450
00:23:30,575 --> 00:23:31,743
See?

451
00:23:33,245 --> 00:23:37,040
Looks like my prayers to
Saint Anthony really worked.

452
00:23:38,834 --> 00:23:40,627
You still managed to find me, bro.

453
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:42,921
- Yeah.
- [Oscar] Right? Oh.

454
00:23:43,004 --> 00:23:44,047
I told you.

455
00:23:44,131 --> 00:23:45,590
But thank you anyway.

456
00:23:45,674 --> 00:23:46,967
I told you, it works.

457
00:23:47,050 --> 00:23:48,218
[Oscar] It has a GPS.

458
00:23:50,554 --> 00:23:51,555
[sighs]

459
00:23:51,638 --> 00:23:53,557
[sentimental music playing]

460
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,559
- Welcome back.
- [chuckles]

461
00:23:55,642 --> 00:24:00,605
- [intense music playing]
- [electronic blipping]

462
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:08,446
What if you're being hasty?

463
00:24:08,530 --> 00:24:10,949
I can't just leave Oka and abandon him.

464
00:24:11,032 --> 00:24:13,285
No family has come to
claim him at the hospital.

465
00:24:13,368 --> 00:24:14,619
[Atoy] <i>He is my friend.</i>

466
00:24:14,703 --> 00:24:16,163
<i>I can't just leave him on his own.</i>

467
00:24:16,246 --> 00:24:18,498
[Audrey] <i>Ten years have passed.</i>

468
00:24:18,582 --> 00:24:22,169
Do you really think he's still
the same Oscar you used to know?

469
00:24:22,252 --> 00:24:23,128
Oh, Ibyang!

470
00:24:23,879 --> 00:24:25,172
Ibyang, come here!

471
00:24:25,255 --> 00:24:27,132
- I don’t, I don't--
- Get out of my house!

472
00:24:27,215 --> 00:24:28,258
You are shameless!

473
00:24:28,341 --> 00:24:29,551
<i>It's a mother's instinct.</i>

474
00:24:29,634 --> 00:24:30,927
You have to trust me!

475
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:32,679
You're just
misinterpreting things. Okay?

476
00:24:32,762 --> 00:24:35,223
You know what that
mother's instinct of yours is?

477
00:24:35,307 --> 00:24:36,558
It's bias!

478
00:24:36,641 --> 00:24:38,476
Because you never really wanted
Oka to stay here, right?

479
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:39,561
Yes! I don't want him here!

480
00:24:39,644 --> 00:24:42,480
- [Atoy] <i>There! See?</i>
- <i>Because I don't trust that man!</i>

481
00:24:43,481 --> 00:24:45,400
[Oscar] <i>I will make sure</i>
<i>all of that happens, Audrey.</i>

482
00:24:45,483 --> 00:24:48,570
And there’s nothing Atoy can do about it.

483
00:24:48,653 --> 00:24:50,614
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

484
00:24:55,076 --> 00:24:56,536
Rachel C. Arias: Script Producer
Closed Caption Transcriptionist
